\b\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid5260211\charrsid5260211  }{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid5260211\charrsid5260211 What is the effect of an increase in potential output on inflation and output?}{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid5260211 
\par }{\f1\cf0\highlight7\ulc0\insrsid6817548\charrsid6817548 Solution:-}{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6817548 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6817548 {\b\f0\cf2\ulc0\insrsid6817548\charrsid6817548    }{\b\f0\ul\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6817548\charrsid6817548 The Effects of an increase in potential Output on Inflation and Output}{
\f0\ul\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6817548\charrsid6817548  
\par }{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6817548\charrsid6817548 
An increase in potential output shifts the LRAS curve to the right. In the short run, current output remains unchanged. But since current output is now below potential output, the resulting recessionary gap places downward pressure on inflation and output
 eventually begin to rise.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6817548\charrsid5260211 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid5260211\charrsid5260211     }{\b\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid5260211\charrsid5260211 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid5260211\charrsid5260211 Question No: 50    ( Marks: 3 ) 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid2125309\charrsid5260211 {\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1074{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}
